WEBVTT

00:02.090 --> 00:03.990
Man, the weather’s really great.

00:03.990 --> 00:08.690
When you have a day off this great,
you want a nice walk, you know?

00:08.690 --> 00:15.350
I’d like to go with Ayako-san, if possible.
Wait, what’s this bad feeling?

00:15.350 --> 00:18.930
Actually, it’s a very icky feeling...

00:36.140 --> 00:41.260
Today I shout out another good morning courageously

00:41.260 --> 00:46.560
The sparkling chime of hope is resounding

00:47.050 --> 00:52.140
The gentle sun is always

00:52.140 --> 00:57.660
Blessing the late coming sensation of the two of them

00:57.950 --> 01:02.880
To fall in love with a goddess is the best!

01:03.090 --> 01:12.950
Even if she is a beatrice I can't control this throbbing feeling

01:12.950 --> 01:13.800
L·O·V·E

01:13.800 --> 01:15.550
I love you MA·MO·RU!

01:15.550 --> 01:17.090
These overflowing feelings

01:17.090 --> 01:19.790
Take them high into the sky

01:19.790 --> 01:24.680
Please grant me my dazzling and sparkling dream

01:24.680 --> 01:26.480
That's right MA·MO·RU!

01:26.480 --> 01:28.010
Only for you

01:28.010 --> 01:30.680
I will show you my power of miracles

01:30.680 --> 01:32.950
I will surely, surely swear

01:32.950 --> 01:38.900
I will not end my Shining Love

01:51.880 --> 01:57.710
Boss, don’t forget us!

01:57.710 --> 02:02.660
Boss, it was short, but thanks
for taking care of us!

02:02.660 --> 02:06.980
Not at all. I’m very grateful,
as well, Jirou, Saburou.

02:07.700 --> 02:10.850
Thank you for everything.

02:18.660 --> 02:20.360
Kikukawa, stop the car.

02:21.950 --> 02:24.250
Boss... Boss!

02:24.250 --> 02:27.920
Jirou, Saburou, don’t cry so much.

02:27.920 --> 02:30.670
I’ll end up taking your tears.

02:30.670 --> 02:33.790
You mean you’ll start crying, too!

02:33.790 --> 02:37.910
Really? I tried to make it a bit more formal.

02:37.910 --> 02:40.500
Japanese is pretty complicated.

02:40.500 --> 02:43.220
Jirou, Saburou, thanks for sticking
with me to the end.

02:43.220 --> 02:45.920
Don’t say the end!

02:54.560 --> 02:56.480
Emelenzia...

02:56.480 --> 02:58.400
You’re going back to Germany, aren’t you?

03:08.230 --> 03:09.720
Witch Beatrice...

03:10.620 --> 03:15.650
Aim To Be a High School Girl!?

03:23.620 --> 03:24.660
Witch Beatrice...

03:24.660 --> 03:26.320
What is it?

03:27.720 --> 03:32.000
I have something to ask you...

03:32.000 --> 03:32.850
To ask me?

03:34.130 --> 03:38.840
Please teach me Japanese culture.

03:38.840 --> 03:43.090
What? Why do you want me to teach you?

03:48.530 --> 03:50.050
<i>Emelenzia...</i>

03:51.680 --> 03:54.590
<i>A lot did happen with her...</i>

03:56.800 --> 04:01.300
<i>I guess, before she leaves, I should at least
give her some good memories of Japan.</i>

04:03.520 --> 04:04.700
I have it.

04:05.800 --> 04:07.780
Danke, Witch Beatrice!

04:07.780 --> 04:09.180
I thank you!

04:10.340 --> 04:13.960
You say Japanese culture, but there’s a lot to it.

04:13.960 --> 04:16.580
What, exactly, are you looking for?

04:16.580 --> 04:19.440
I... Um...

04:20.330 --> 04:22.500
H-High school girls.

04:24.820 --> 04:28.230
Huh? High school girls?!

04:35.080 --> 04:38.680
Anyway, so I had you all come.

04:38.680 --> 04:41.170
You did, huh?

04:41.170 --> 04:42.980
But it’s a good thing.

04:42.980 --> 04:44.520
So we’ll definitely...

04:44.520 --> 04:46.930
help you. Emelenzia-san?

04:46.930 --> 04:47.510
Yes?

04:47.510 --> 04:49.980
Ahem. We’ll set up the...

04:49.980 --> 04:51.140
make Emelenzia-san...

04:51.140 --> 04:52.290
a wonderful...

04:52.290 --> 04:53.870
high school girl...

04:53.870 --> 04:55.410
committee.

04:55.410 --> 04:57.250
Right!

04:58.070 --> 05:00.210
Thank you.

05:00.210 --> 05:01.950
Welcome.

05:01.950 --> 05:03.920
Welcome, Mamoru.

05:04.760 --> 05:09.290
Sorry for asking you here.
I remembered your house was nearby.

05:09.920 --> 05:13.380
Today’s our Sit-Down Restaurant
Research Club meeting.

05:13.380 --> 05:15.260
Sit-Down Restaurant Research Club...

05:15.260 --> 05:16.680
Shh!

05:17.440 --> 05:18.040
Sit-Down Restaurant Research Club

05:18.530 --> 05:22.550
I see. I didn’t know there was one.

05:22.940 --> 05:25.890
Our goal is to try everything on every menu!

05:25.890 --> 05:29.650
But the road to that goal is,
without doubt, a difficult one!

05:29.650 --> 05:31.980
I guess that’s why it’s worth doing!

05:31.980 --> 05:32.520
I see...

05:32.520 --> 05:35.150
How about it? You wanna join, too?

05:35.150 --> 05:38.290
If you join now, you’ll get some coupons.
It’s a real bargain.

05:38.290 --> 05:40.460
Welcome!

05:42.800 --> 05:44.700
Thank you...

05:44.700 --> 05:45.730
Good.

05:48.370 --> 05:49.830
But Mamoru-kun,

05:49.830 --> 05:53.920
it’s Sunday, and you have the day off.
Why aren’t you with Ayako?

05:53.920 --> 05:54.970
That’s because...

05:53.920 --> 05:54.970
The best!

05:55.800 --> 05:58.670
It’s an all-girl thing today.

05:58.670 --> 06:03.210
You say all-girl, but they’re really in
their secret garden together!

06:05.920 --> 06:08.110
A-Abiko-sempai.

06:08.110 --> 06:09.400
He showed up again...

06:09.400 --> 06:10.890
Wh-Why are you here?

06:10.890 --> 06:14.990
Wherever Yoshimura Mamoru is, Ayako-san is there!

06:14.990 --> 06:17.900
Did you follow Mamoru-kun?

06:17.900 --> 06:19.600
Indeed.

06:19.600 --> 06:20.900
When?

06:22.730 --> 06:26.020
I’ll show you, this one time!

06:29.580 --> 06:31.760
You’re acting like a stalker.

06:31.760 --> 06:33.410
It’s like pictures of ghosts.

06:34.660 --> 06:37.040
Well, anyway, that’s what happened.

06:37.550 --> 06:38.870
That’s kind of...

06:40.270 --> 06:43.190
Anyway, since you’re here, why not sit with us?

06:43.190 --> 06:46.900
I can’t sit at the same table as my enemy!

06:46.900 --> 06:48.520
I-I’m an enemy?

06:48.520 --> 06:50.900
You understand, Yoshimura Mamoru!

06:50.900 --> 06:52.280
That’s right!

06:52.280 --> 06:55.840
The love triangle that revolves around Ayako-san. Not the trigonometric functions,

06:55.840 --> 06:58.200
but rather, the two of points on that triangle!

06:59.350 --> 07:02.480
Are we not enemies?

07:04.790 --> 07:06.890
Well, there’s no helping that.

07:06.890 --> 07:10.730
Anyway, Mamoru-kun, what are Ayako
and the others doing, without us guys?

07:10.730 --> 07:13.980
Well, she wouldn’t tell me.

07:13.980 --> 07:18.220
She just said she was only
spending time with the girls today.

07:18.220 --> 07:21.830
O-Only with the girls...

07:23.990 --> 07:26.190
Youko, your breasts are really big!

07:26.190 --> 07:28.000
Stop that, Mitsuki.

07:28.000 --> 07:30.140
Hey, Yuuka, what do you think?

07:30.140 --> 07:32.710
Anna, they’re very cute and sexy.

07:32.710 --> 07:34.640
I got your bra, Ayako.

07:34.640 --> 07:36.190
Hey!

07:37.810 --> 07:40.080
How nice...

07:40.080 --> 07:40.640
Huh?

07:42.810 --> 07:45.150
Macho man.

07:44.160 --> 07:45.150
What?

07:49.530 --> 07:51.720
I heard that Japanese high school girls
create Japanese culture.

07:51.720 --> 07:53.590
That’s right.

07:53.590 --> 07:59.030
I thought I should understand high school
girls first, to understand Japan.

07:59.030 --> 08:01.850
Yep, that’s a good idea.

08:01.850 --> 08:02.830
Isn’t it?

08:02.830 --> 08:05.040
Really?

08:05.040 --> 08:09.200
I thought it’d be best to ask
high school girls about high school girls.

08:09.200 --> 08:11.630
And I asked Witch Beatrice for help.

08:11.630 --> 08:14.750
You might have approached it from the wrong angle.

08:14.750 --> 08:19.480
The wrong angle? How was I supposed to measure it?

08:19.480 --> 08:23.270
No, she’s saying you asked
precisely the wrong person.

08:23.270 --> 08:26.670
Asking Ayako for help won’t do you any good.

08:26.670 --> 08:30.990
Ayako’s about the furthest you can get
from a normal high school girl.

08:31.300 --> 08:34.270
That’s going too far, Shione!

08:34.270 --> 08:36.170
And what do you mean by that?!

08:36.170 --> 08:40.340
I mean a normal high school girl
wouldn’t wipe out her school!

08:40.340 --> 08:43.970
Well, in order to become
a great high school girl...

08:43.970 --> 08:47.110
You’ll have to pass some
extremely difficult challenges!

08:47.110 --> 08:48.280
Huh?

08:48.280 --> 08:51.880
Are you prepared?

08:54.350 --> 08:57.940
I believe I am!

08:58.770 --> 09:02.860
No matter what type of training I must endure,

09:02.860 --> 09:04.710
I want to...

09:09.360 --> 09:13.070
To become a better high school girl
than everyone else!

09:15.260 --> 09:16.620
I understand!

09:16.620 --> 09:18.810
We of Tobi University High School,

09:18.810 --> 09:20.510
the female student council members,

09:20.510 --> 09:22.420
will bestow upon you the knowledge

09:22.420 --> 09:24.220
of Japanese high school girls!

09:24.220 --> 09:25.950
Please do!

09:25.950 --> 09:28.250
Tobi Girls, fight!

09:29.250 --> 09:32.600
<i>She really isn’t planning anything?</i>

09:35.040 --> 09:37.700
Is this a café?

09:37.700 --> 09:41.340
It’s a butler café.

09:41.340 --> 09:42.180
I see.

09:42.180 --> 09:45.900
They have goats here. They like to head-butt...

09:47.910 --> 09:51.110
That was a very old joke...

09:52.500 --> 09:55.230
They’re really popular right now,
between high school girls.

09:55.230 --> 09:59.290
If you come here, you can be a princess.
That’s what they’re for.

09:59.290 --> 10:00.580
I see.

10:00.580 --> 10:05.220
Japan’s high school girls spend
their afternoons like this.

10:05.220 --> 10:07.520
Not all of them!

10:07.520 --> 10:08.480
Here you go.

10:08.480 --> 10:10.000
Thank you.

10:11.330 --> 10:16.300
Once it’s time to go horseback riding, I’ll let you know.

10:16.300 --> 10:18.900
I know a bit about riding.

10:18.900 --> 10:22.020
Oh, really? I, also, know how to ride horses.

10:22.020 --> 10:23.970
This is difficult to express, Witch Beatrice,

10:23.970 --> 10:28.040
but since early childhood, I’ve ridden
horses through Germany’s forests.

10:28.040 --> 10:29.360
I believe I’d be more skilled.

10:29.360 --> 10:30.430
What are you saying?

10:29.360 --> 10:30.490
Hey, there...

10:30.430 --> 10:32.750
They don’t understand anything, do they?

10:32.750 --> 10:35.720
Hey! Hurry and bring out the horse!

10:35.720 --> 10:37.430
Please bring the horse!

10:37.430 --> 10:38.120
Huh?

10:38.680 --> 10:40.990
Like hell they have one.

10:42.350 --> 10:45.530
Karaoke is pretty obvious for a high school girl.

10:45.530 --> 10:50.510
But I’ve never sung in front of people before.

10:50.510 --> 10:52.870
If you don’t, you can’t be a good high school girl.

10:52.870 --> 10:55.540
You want to be a high school girl, don’t you?

10:55.540 --> 10:57.470
I understand.

10:58.620 --> 11:02.780
I’ll sing to be a good high school girl!

11:02.780 --> 11:04.390
A Maiden’s Heart Is a Sachertorte

11:08.000 --> 11:09.450
Do your best.

11:10.350 --> 11:17.400
<i>Until I’m able to capture your heart,</i>

11:17.400 --> 11:23.640
<i>I’ll lock-on, ready to fire.</i>

11:21.880 --> 11:23.950
She’s rather good.

11:23.950 --> 11:26.410
It doesn’t seem like this is her first time at all.

11:24.270 --> 11:27.370
<i>Non! Non! It’s not strange at all.</i>

11:27.370 --> 11:31.210
<i>No one understands why</i>

11:31.210 --> 11:34.380
<i>I’m not lonely at all.</i>

11:34.740 --> 11:39.420
<i>Playfully dancing...</i>

11:40.020 --> 11:46.720
<i>My heart is a Sachertorte.</i>

11:53.070 --> 11:55.090
Pretty impressive.

11:55.090 --> 11:57.000
Really?

11:58.780 --> 12:00.270
Huh? What’s that?

12:04.780 --> 12:06.500
Ayako’s going to sing?

12:06.500 --> 12:08.180
It’s her first time.

12:08.180 --> 12:11.190
Just shut up and listen.

12:10.350 --> 12:12.220
Night Upon Umihotaru

12:12.220 --> 12:23.220
<i>The man who gently melted the shell
of stubbornness surrounding her.</i>

12:23.220 --> 12:33.350
<i>It’s so embarrassing... It feels like I’m going crazy, but I want to give you everything.</i>

12:33.350 --> 12:36.160
<i>I return your embrace.</i>

12:36.160 --> 12:39.110
<i>The waves soak me.</i>

12:36.750 --> 12:38.720
She’s pretty good.

12:38.720 --> 12:39.650
Y-Yeah.

12:39.650 --> 12:52.280
<i>Night upon Umihotaru.</i>

12:51.690 --> 12:53.290
Pretty good, Witch Beatrice.

12:56.430 --> 12:57.940
You both scored the same.

12:57.940 --> 12:59.270
You’ve gotta be kidding.

12:59.270 --> 13:01.740
Just now, I was much better.

13:01.740 --> 13:06.440
Really? Musically, I think my
singing was much better.

13:06.440 --> 13:07.650
What was that?

13:07.650 --> 13:09.140
Then let’s go again!

13:09.140 --> 13:10.270
You’ve got it.

13:11.160 --> 13:13.730
I wonder why they’re fighting so much.

13:13.730 --> 13:16.230
It’s fun just watching them.

13:16.230 --> 13:20.150
If you’re a high school girl,
you’ve gotta take photo booth pictures!

13:21.130 --> 13:22.620
Huh? You’re already taking one?

13:22.620 --> 13:25.020
I understand. A picture to remember
everything by, right?

13:25.020 --> 13:27.280
Hey! Don’t hog the whole frame!

13:27.280 --> 13:28.650
You, too, Witch Beatrice!

13:28.650 --> 13:29.960
Cheese!

13:30.630 --> 13:34.180
Anyway, Emelenzia, how about this?

13:35.000 --> 13:38.750
I think a noble smile like that looks good on you.

13:38.750 --> 13:42.770
I think a more natural smile
would look good on you here.

13:42.770 --> 13:43.780
Now you’ve done it!

13:43.780 --> 13:45.260
How about that?

13:45.260 --> 13:47.210
I’ll do the same!

13:47.210 --> 13:49.850
What are you doing?!

13:54.930 --> 13:56.790
We’re finally here.

13:57.350 --> 13:59.420
This is the final trial.

13:59.420 --> 14:01.670
High school girls like fashion!

14:01.670 --> 14:05.400
Emelenzia-kun, show me what it
means to be a high school girl!

14:05.400 --> 14:06.160
Yes!

14:13.000 --> 14:17.070
I’ll let you know when it’s time for the ball.

14:17.070 --> 14:21.750
Th-This butler café is really popular
right now with the girls.

14:22.340 --> 14:24.350
It seems that high school girls are attracted

14:24.350 --> 14:26.670
to the gentlemanly attitudes displayed here.

14:26.670 --> 14:28.960
I see.

14:30.890 --> 14:33.190
Please request something

14:32.200 --> 14:37.580
It seems that currently, the popular guys
can sing anything a girl might request.

14:37.580 --> 14:39.300
I see.

14:41.960 --> 14:46.320
Photo booths are really popular with girls now.

14:46.320 --> 14:47.720
I see...

14:51.690 --> 14:56.970
And girls are absolutely into guys with fashion sense.

15:00.260 --> 15:03.250
I’ve had enough!

15:02.850 --> 15:03.670
What’s wrong?

15:03.670 --> 15:06.090
Yoshimura, you have Takasu!

15:06.590 --> 15:09.460
The President is handsome and plenty popular.

15:09.960 --> 15:12.730
Yagi’s not interested in anything but his own muscles!

15:13.230 --> 15:15.640
Abiko has so many problems...

15:15.640 --> 15:17.530
Anyway, I’ve had enough!

15:17.530 --> 15:21.340
I want to fall in love!

15:21.340 --> 15:24.710
I want to run straight into a new romance!

15:24.710 --> 15:26.460
Be careful!

15:26.460 --> 15:28.590
A newcomer running in there alone is dangerous!

15:29.460 --> 15:31.380
Watanabe!

15:33.830 --> 15:36.120
Meeting someone new, huh?

15:39.990 --> 15:41.540
No, no.

15:41.540 --> 15:42.170
Not this.

15:42.170 --> 15:42.850
Not this, either.

15:44.210 --> 15:45.830
No, no!

15:45.830 --> 15:47.550
I can’t win with this.

15:47.550 --> 15:49.700
I can’t win!

15:50.370 --> 15:52.840
Aren’t they after something else?

15:52.840 --> 15:55.260
She said she wanted to be a
great high school student...

15:55.690 --> 15:56.810
Yeah, she did, didn’t she?

15:57.430 --> 15:58.430
Yeah...

16:10.760 --> 16:12.170
What’s that about?

16:12.170 --> 16:14.230
You went through all that trouble,
and that’s what you got?

16:14.230 --> 16:16.120
You’re doing this on purpose, aren’t you?

16:26.230 --> 16:29.940
You can’t think just because
you’re young, you can show skin.

16:34.770 --> 16:36.750
That’s great.

16:37.930 --> 16:39.650
Y-You’re definitely a high school girl.

16:39.650 --> 16:41.070
Yeah, ha ha.

16:41.950 --> 16:43.720
Watanabe, you—

16:43.720 --> 16:45.290
Huh?

16:45.290 --> 16:45.970
Oh.

16:45.970 --> 16:46.520
My.

16:47.250 --> 16:51.170
Sorry. Huh? Ayako-san?

16:51.890 --> 16:53.700
M-Mamoru?

16:58.870 --> 17:00.380
Wait, Ayak-san!

17:00.380 --> 17:01.660
Don’t do it, Ayako-san!

17:01.660 --> 17:02.670
Witch Beatrice.

17:02.670 --> 17:04.440
She’s...

17:04.440 --> 17:09.680
Don’t look!

17:08.140 --> 17:09.680
Ayako-san!

17:23.410 --> 17:24.920
Emelenzia-san.

17:28.900 --> 17:30.630
Shione-san...

17:31.510 --> 17:35.700
Why were you fighting with Ayako so much?

17:37.240 --> 17:38.610
I...

17:38.610 --> 17:43.650
I wanted to be like her.

17:44.820 --> 17:50.750
She was the first ideal person
I’d met, after my brother.

17:52.590 --> 17:54.420
I wanted to catch up to her.

17:54.420 --> 17:56.690
I wanted to be accepted by her.

17:57.290 --> 17:59.370
That’s why I became stronger.

18:00.030 --> 18:06.060
Witch Beatrice is my goal,
the person I must eventually surpass...

18:06.060 --> 18:09.670
A summit much higher than Mt. Fuji’s.

18:10.660 --> 18:12.230
I see.

18:12.230 --> 18:13.430
That’s what it was.

18:14.680 --> 18:18.520
What you say is very wonderful,

18:18.520 --> 18:21.450
but the way you’re fighting is idiotic!

18:23.870 --> 18:26.530
Please forget!

18:26.530 --> 18:28.160
Please!

18:28.890 --> 18:31.210
It was a mistake.

18:31.210 --> 18:33.960
It’s fine. I’ve already forgotten.

18:34.440 --> 18:36.620
You’re lying!

18:41.940 --> 18:45.770
Thank you for everything you did today.

18:45.770 --> 18:47.070
Same here.

18:47.070 --> 18:50.580
I feel like I’m really a
high school girl, in body and mind.

18:50.580 --> 18:51.950
Here, take this.

18:51.950 --> 18:53.300
What is it?

18:53.300 --> 18:54.320
A gift.

18:54.320 --> 18:55.320
Eat it.

18:55.320 --> 18:58.660
Thank you, Witch Beatrice.

19:01.310 --> 19:03.810
These are beatrice cookies, aren’t they?

19:03.810 --> 19:08.010
They’re famous in Hakata,
but they’re sold at Tobi-U for some reason.

19:08.010 --> 19:09.770
She sure knows a lot about weird stuff.

19:12.720 --> 19:14.090
Witch Beatrice.

19:14.090 --> 19:15.960
Wh-What?

19:15.960 --> 19:18.610
I’m glad I met you.

19:21.070 --> 19:22.370
Stay well.

19:22.370 --> 19:23.470
You, too.

19:32.550 --> 19:37.430
<i>Let’s meet again, Emelenzia Beatrix Rudiger.</i>

19:44.230 --> 19:45.910
Y-You’re...

19:51.930 --> 19:53.210
Good morning.

19:53.210 --> 19:55.040
Good morning, both of you.

19:55.040 --> 19:56.180
It’s a nice morning, today.

19:56.180 --> 19:59.950
Why are you wearing that uniform,
when it doesn’t even fit?!

20:00.850 --> 20:02.590
It doesn’t look good on me?

20:02.590 --> 20:05.040
That isn’t the point!

20:05.040 --> 20:10.280
I think she wants to know why
you’re wearing our uniform.

20:10.280 --> 20:12.720
Because I transferred in.

20:12.720 --> 20:14.100
Transferred in?

20:14.100 --> 20:16.290
More specifically, she’s studying abroad.

20:16.290 --> 20:19.210
They’re treating her as if she had
an Aldemar University scholarship.

20:19.210 --> 20:21.070
Anyway, get along well.

20:21.070 --> 20:24.880
I’m a Japanese high school girl now.

20:24.880 --> 20:27.400
This is why you wanted to be a high school girl!

20:28.160 --> 20:31.020
Then why were those two idiots crying?

20:32.360 --> 20:36.910
Because if she starts going to school, we can’t be with her during lunch!

20:36.910 --> 20:40.090
We don’t want to be separated from her for a second!

20:42.660 --> 20:45.890
How stupid. They made everyone worry!

20:47.970 --> 20:51.710
If you’re upset and hungry,
how about a beatrice cookie?

20:51.710 --> 20:52.640
They’re very good.

20:52.640 --> 20:54.290
I don’t need any!

20:54.290 --> 20:55.790
Ayako-san...

20:55.790 --> 20:57.340
Yoshimura Mamoru...

20:57.340 --> 20:58.650
Yes?

20:59.200 --> 21:01.650
It’ll be nice to spend time with you.

21:03.480 --> 21:06.250
Yeah. For me, too.

21:15.830 --> 21:19.110
Your smile is mine alone.

21:19.110 --> 21:19.970
Huh?

21:22.150 --> 21:25.990
<i>Yoshimura Mamoru, what a magnificent smile.</i>

21:38.060 --> 21:41.930
<i>I feel like a storm’s approaching.</i>

22:01.290 --> 22:06.970
My heart is racing and I'm going to give you

22:06.970 --> 22:12.170
This sparkling emotion

22:12.560 --> 22:18.300
The evening color is dyed into this orange shirt

22:18.360 --> 22:23.450
I catch it from behind you and my heart throbbing

22:23.560 --> 22:30.410
It's an everyday thrill just to be with you

22:30.410 --> 22:37.840
I can't say it well enough but thank you

22:37.840 --> 22:43.040
Venus Dream the hidden power

22:43.040 --> 22:49.240
This feeling will change into that power

22:49.240 --> 22:54.360
Power Dream I found what I want to protect

22:54.360 --> 23:00.770
That is your smile and your feelings

23:13.950 --> 23:17.160
Yoshimura Mamoru

23:17.160 --> 23:19.880
I just felt like reading his name.

23:19.880 --> 23:21.000
No real reason.

23:21.000 --> 23:22.710
Get me some juice, Yoshimura Mamoru.

23:21.790 --> 23:22.710
Yoshimura Mamoru

23:22.710 --> 23:26.290
Oh, yeah. Now that I think about it, I haven’t seen many vending machines that give you

23:26.290 --> 23:28.900
a chance to win another bottle each time you buy one.

23:29.330 --> 23:30.350
You joker.

23:31.320 --> 23:33.600
Anyway, as you can tell, this is difficult.

23:33.600 --> 23:35.960
It was one of Shione’s plans that brought

23:35.960 --> 23:37.890
about these difficult previews in the first place.

23:37.890 --> 23:40.850
She may be my sister, but she’s quite the sinful woman.

23:40.170 --> 23:43.980
Operation Cesedu Yoshimura Mamoru!

